  "worked_solution": "In general, congruent polygons have the same shape. In other words:\n\n- they have the same number of sides,\n\n- all corresponding sides are congruent, and\n\n- all corresponding interior angles are congruent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's compare the given polygons.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the polygons $C$ and $V$ have the same number of sides, but they don't seem to have the same shape. In particular, we notice they don't have corresponding congruent sides.\n\n- Statement II is false. By the same reasoning as statement I, we can see that the polygons $V$ and $B$ are not congruent.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the polygons $B$ and $C$ have the same number of sides and all corresponding sides and angles are congruent, we conclude that $B≅C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
